% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `as_resource`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: the class is
% lost, and no body of it is printed.  Step 3j.  Every method is
% INTERPOLATED.
%
% What is PRINTED:
%   - TM-065 p13: `file` has the natures as_resource and with_lock (name
%     only; docs/simpos/printed/NAMED_NOT_DEFINED.md);
%   - TM-100 Fig. 3.1 (PDF p8): the process instance slot `resources`, a
%     list (`( resources := List :- :create(#list, List) )`);
%   - TR-285 PDF p11 (folio 8), page image read 2026-11-25: "closing open
%     files and releasing locked semaphores on unexpected process
%     termination are effected by the same invocation of the same method,
%     in the process management module, of different objects."  So a
%     process holds its resource objects, and they are cleaned up with it
%     (the method is not named; not stood in).
% What is HELD:
%   - pimscsi##pseudo_scsi (natures keyed_message, as_resource,
%     as_class_with_lock; compiled, source not held): create/4 sends
%     `:assign(Obj)` to the new object (@71); close/1 (@150-16d) is
%     `( :assigned(Self), !, ..., Self!status := closed, :resign(Self)
%     ; error(soft, not_assigned, ...) )`, and aborted/1 (@26c) and
%     $or$3/1 (@5bf) test `:assigned(Self)` the same way; the pool string
%     "SCSI is not assigned to process" (pool[2b], used at @56b).  (The
%     pimscsi pools are not relied on in general, psi/fepread/ptfread.py;
%     this string is read as text only.)
%   - HELD-SOURCE, kappa2 tool/kappa_pool/KP_POOL.ESP (nature
%     as_resource): create/4, make/4 and load/4 end with `:assign(Obj)`;
%     terminate/1 and kill/1 end with `:resign(Obj)`; and its local
%     check_resource (:285-290) reads what assign/1 did:
%     `:self(#process,Process), Resource = Process!resources,
%     :get_contents(Resource,R_list)`, then looks in R_list for a
%     kappaITR_application_interface, a class with nature as_resource
%     whose creation sends `:assign(Obj)` (kernel/itr/ITRAPP.ESP:28-33,
%     :106).  Also kernel/dbo/KP_DBOBF.ESP:61-87 (assign, lock, ...,
%     unlock, resign).
% So: assign/1 puts the object in the calling process's `resources`
% list, resign/1 takes it out, assigned/1 succeeds while it is there.
% INTERPOLATED from the above; that `assigned` asks about the CALLING
% process is INFERENCE (the string says only "to process"); appending at
% the end is OURS.  Termination cleanup is not stood in.

class as_resource has

    instance

    % INTERPOLATED: see the header.
    :assign(Resource) :-
        :self(#process, Process),
        :add_last(Process!resources, Resource) ;

    % INTERPOLATED: see the header.  Fails when Resource is not held.
    :assigned(Resource) :-
        :self(#process, Process),
        :get_contents(Process!resources, List),
        held(List, Resource) ;

    % INTERPOLATED: see the header.  Fails when Resource is not held
    % (the list stand-in's remove/2 fails then).
    :resign(Resource) :-
        :self(#process, Process),
        :remove(Process!resources, Resource) ;

    local

    held([R|_], R) :- ! ;
    held([_|L], R) :- held(L, R) ;

end.
